The comparator over runs on disk (compare.in/): a run equal to the oracle's,
and a deliberately divergent fake Rust run, which fails even with its one
approved difference applied. The ledger check fails on a missing field and
on a changelog reference CHANGELOG.md does not hold.

```console
$ xtask compare --oracle oracle --candidate same --command validate --ledger ledger.toml --changelog CHANGELOG.md
compare: `validate` is equal (0 approved difference(s))

$ xtask compare --oracle oracle --candidate fake-rust --command validate --case json/x --ledger ledger.toml --changelog CHANGELOG.md
? 1
error: stdout json_key_order at /summary
  oracle:    errors, files
  candidate: files, errors
error: file:docs/old.md file_extra
  oracle:    (absent)
  candidate: deleted
error: file:docs/rule.md bytes, line 1, byte 2
  oracle:    # Rule
  candidate: # rule
compare: `validate` differs: 3 difference(s), 1 approved

$ xtask compare --check-ledger --ledger ledger.toml --changelog CHANGELOG.md
compare: ledger.toml holds 1 approved difference(s), each with every field

$ xtask compare --check-ledger --ledger no-issue.toml --changelog CHANGELOG.md
? 1
error: no-issue.toml:
missing field `issue` (line 1)

$ xtask compare --check-ledger --ledger unknown-changelog.toml --changelog CHANGELOG.md
? 1
error: unknown-changelog.toml:
entry 1: changelog "**Not in the changelog**" is not in CHANGELOG.md

$ xtask compare --oracle oracle --command validate --ledger ledger.toml --changelog CHANGELOG.md
? 2
xtask compare: --candidate is required

usage: cargo xtask <command> [options]
...

```
